/**
	Look up a material by name.
	physics_material@ physics_material_get(const string&in name);
	## Arguments:
		* const string&in name: the name of the material.
	## Returns:
		physics_material@: the material, or null if no material has that name.
	## Remarks:
		A physics_material describes a kind of surface. Bodies created from a shape that has a material start with the material's friction and restitution, and its acoustic properties control how sound is absorbed, scattered and let through it in acoustic simulations such as the nvgt_phonon plugin's sound_environment. Give one to a shape when you create it.
		These materials are built in: generic, brick, concrete, ceramic, gravel, carpet, glass, plaster, wood, metal, rock, sand, snow, soil, foliage, water, drywall, marble, asphalt, grass, fabric, cardboard, plastic, rubber, foam and ice. `physics_material_list()` returns the names of every material that exists, including those you register yourself.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	physics_material@ wood = physics_material_get("wood");
	if (wood is null) return;
	alert("Wood", "Wood has a friction of " + wood.friction + " and a restitution of " + wood.restitution + ".");
}
